      "assertion_level": "author_interpretation",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "page": 2,
          "section": "Introduction",
          "quote": "A recent study has revealed that dynamic embrittlement in Ni-based superalloys can be mitigated and suppressed by the formation of common oxides such as Cr2O3 and Al2O3 that exhibit large transformation strains and induced large compressive stresses ahead of the crack tip or in the crack wake.",
